ak point left beside Black's stones on C2 and C1."}, {"turn": 39, "text": "The 20k's B5 answered at once and lost 32.0 points, dropping the lead from +32.1 to +0.1. The engine's choice was D2 here too, so both players walked past the same point."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "A2 lost 10.0 points, and it followed A4 (12.2 lost) and the 20k's A5 (12.2 lost) on the left edge. After the 20k's E2 at move 43 the score settled at about Black +10, and neither side moved it again."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either called go tools to play a move the player had already chosen, or ran the inspection and verification code (game-078-inspection.js, game-078-verification.js), which only parse the supplied board, count groups, liberties and area, and replay the recorded history. The remaining commands counted a hand-written list of 42 target points, built the SGF and notes, and wrote and re-read files. None of it looped over candidate moves, ranked moves, or played out future sequences.", "stop": false}}